+Generated using the built-in image_gen tool from text only. No reference images were supplied.
+
+917-sgraffito.png
+Create one fresh image from text only, square 1024x1024. No reference images. Use case: stylized-concept. Authentic SGRAFFITO WALL artwork: colored plaster scratched away to reveal contrasting colored plaster underneath, every mark materially cut into plaster, not ink, not a photograph with a filter. A large exuberant stylized full-body female figure occupies almost the whole rough wall, in an asymmetrical seated side-profile composition, with decorative flattened folk-mural proportions. The woman is in her early 30s, with curly auburn shoulder-length hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses, and a mustard-yellow knit sweater, enjoying a coffee with a croissant nearby. Express these identity features using plaster layers and scratched patterns, including auburn curlicue hair, scratched freckles, circular glasses, and rhythmic scratched sweater stitches. Exactly TWO arms and TWO legs, each anatomically unambiguous and visible; one arm bends to bring the scratched coffee cup to her mouth, her other hand rests on her bent knee. Both legs extend in different directions as an expressive seated mural pose. A croissant is scratched into the wall close beside her on a simple scratched ledge. Broad earthy rust, mustard ochre, cream and dark plaster underlayers; visibly scraped edges, granules, tool chatter, chips, weathered pitted stucco. Raking natural daylight makes tiny incised shadows. Everything depicting woman, coffee and croissant is scratched plaster. Style determines anatomy and composition. No painted realistic woman, no ink, no written graffiti, no lettering, no text, no caption, no signature, no watermark.
+
+918-orrery.png
+Create one fresh image from text only, square 1024x1024. No reference images. Use case: stylized-concept. An authentic eighteenth-century ORRERY constructed as ONE large female figure, a sculptural astronomical automaton made entirely of brass rings, intricate gears, enamel spheres and mechanical linkages. Three-quarter low viewpoint, full standing figure including feet on an elegant wooden base, in a dark unlit study with a single warm shaft of window light; generous dark negative space around elaborate orbital silhouette. This is an actual coherent antique instrument whose architecture IS the woman, not a human beside a machine or a person with a brass filter. Exactly TWO brass arms and exactly TWO brass legs, unmistakable and separated; rings remain circular internal torso framework, never extra limbs. One arm bends up to lift a tiny brass coffee cup near her mouth, the other bends across the torso supporting a small brass croissant amongst the orbital rings. The character represented is a woman in her early 30s, curly auburn shoulder-length hair as tightly wound reddish-copper spirals framing an enamel face, tiny freckle speckles in enamel, round tortoiseshell-pattern spectacle rims, and a mustard-yellow knit sweater interpreted as ochre-yellow enamel torso segments with precise interlocking knit-pattern metalwork over the gears. All limbs are brass. Small enamel planets, fine gear teeth, patinated brass and brown polished wood. Proportions follow whimsical period scientific instrument craftsmanship, long elegant articulated legs and open celestial globe chest. Dramatic dimensional chiaroscuro and museum-object material authenticity. No extra arms or legs, no extra figures, no writing, no engraved words, no letters, no numbers, no caption, no signature, no watermark.
+
+919-tangram.png
+Generate a fresh square image, 1024x1024, with NO reference image. Authentic austere TANGRAM puzzle art. Exactly SEVEN separate solid jet-black polygons on a solid opaque ivory-white background, clearly visible and countable, generous empty margin. NOT transparent. This is a highly abstract silhouette of one woman leaning forward to enjoy coffee, viewed in profile. Exactly two arms and two legs. Use ONLY these seven single-piece shapes, no subdivisions: 1. one tilted SQUARE for the head; 2. one MEDIUM TRIANGLE for the torso/sweater; 3. one PARALLELOGRAM projecting up from the torso for the arm reaching toward her face; 4. one SMALL TRIANGLE projecting from the opposite side of the torso for her other arm, this triangle also suggests the nearby croissant; 5. one LARGE TRIANGLE projecting downward for the first leg; 6. one LARGE TRIANGLE projecting downward at a different angle for the second leg; 7. one SMALL TRIANGLE between the raised arm tip and the face, suggesting her coffee cup. All seven shapes together form the single coherent angular woman. Coffee and croissant exist WITHIN the seven polygons, not as additional shapes. Narrow white gaps separate the seven pieces; every piece is entirely black, no outlines, no holes, no shading. Do not divide either leg or arm into segments. No separate hands, no separate feet. Character concept: woman early 30s, shoulder-length curly auburn hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses, mustard-yellow knit sweater, enjoying coffee with croissant nearby; interpret her as radically abstract black tangram shapes, the medium overrides literal details and colors. NO face details, curls, glasses outlines, sweater stitches or extra marks. No furniture, no steam, no shadow, no background objects. No text, numbers, captions, signature or watermark. Count exactly SEVEN black shapes, no more.
+
+920-manhole.png
+Create one fresh image from text only, square 1024x1024. No reference images. Use case: stylized-concept. A massive circular CAST-IRON MANHOLE COVER seen precisely straight down from above, filling the square frame edge to edge with only narrow gritty stone corners. The cover features an authentic bold low CAST RELIEF of ONE large full-body woman integrated into the industrial foundry design, plus strong radial reinforcing ribs around the perimeter. The figure uses compact, thick, rounded, foreshortened foundry-relief proportions, front-facing in the circular center, seated with two knees apart and two stubby feet, not a realistic portrait and not a photo with a style filter. Exactly TWO arms and TWO legs, cast as clear readable shapes. One hand raises a cast-relief coffee cup to her mouth; her other hand rests beside a separate clearly recognizable crescent-shaped cast croissant nearby on a tiny integrated relief ledge. The represented woman is early 30s, with shoulder-length curly auburn hair indicated through clustered cast spiral locks, freckles cast as tiny shallow pits on cheeks, round tortoiseshell glasses represented by thick raised circular spectacle rims with speckled casting, and mustard-yellow knit sweater represented by raised chevron knit ridges and a subtle worn yellow-ochre patina only on the sweater relief. Hair can have traces of warm reddish-brown iron oxidation. Most of the artwork is heavy charcoal-black cast iron. Wet metal gleams in overcast daylight, droplets and shallow puddles catch silver highlights, dirt and grit pack the deep recessed areas, worn raised edges shine. Radial ribs are industrial structure and never additional arms or legs. Sculpture and material dictate anatomy, perspective and details. No extra figures or limbs. Absolutely no city name, no lettering, no words, no letters, no numbers, no text, no caption, no signature, no watermark.
+

